[B]About[/B]

Unofficial CyanogenMod 10 (Android 4.1.2 Jelly Bean) port for the LG L4 II E440g, codename [B]vee4ss[/B], SoC MediaTek MT6575 — the same platform family as the already-more-mature [B]vee5ss[/B] (LG L5 II) port, and based directly on that device tree.

This build uses the stock prebuilt kernel and a MediaTek-format boot image generated with [B]mtkbootimg[/B]. The OTA zip updates [B]/system only[/B] — you must flash [B]boot.img separately[/B] via dd (see install instructions).

[B]Device specs[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Device: LG L4 II / LG-E440g
[*]Codename: vee4ss
[*]SoC: MediaTek MT6575, ARMv7-A Cortex-A9
[*]Display: 3.2" 320×480 HVGA mdpi, command-mode DSI panel (ili9486)
[*]Android: 4.1.2 Jelly Bean (JZO54K)
[/LIST]

[B]Current status (2026-07-30)[/B]

Early alpha. Core system, display, and Bluetooth are confirmed working. Audio (playback and recording) was completely broken until this build and is now confirmed working, including in-app video recording — though recording still has a known stability bug (see below). Telephony is NOT yet functional.

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Boots to Android (sys.boot_completed=1), consistent/reproducible boot
[*]Display + touchscreen — required a custom MTK HWC/GraphicBuffer ABI compatibility shim (this device's proprietary graphics blobs use MediaTek extensions to the stock JB HWC ABI)
[*]Boot animation (320×320)
[*]SurfaceFlinger, Launcher, Settings, core apps
[*]Bluetooth (MT6620, MediaTek BlueAngel stack, not stock BlueZ) — confirmed STATE_OFF→ON→OFF cycle, correct controller address, classic discovery finds real devices with SDP UUIDs
[*]WiFi (MT6620) — confirmed working
[*]ADB reliable across reboots
[*]Internal storage + external microSD
[*]Torch / flashlight (via Camera interface)
[*]Audio output AND input — [B]both were completely non-functional until this build[/B] (see Known bugs history); now load and work correctly
[*]Camera preview
[*]Video recording with audio — starts, records, produces a playable file for several seconds (see known bug below for the current limit)
[/LIST]

[B]Not tested / pending[/B]
[LIST]
[*]SMS
[*]Mobile data
[*]GPS
[*]Camera still-photo capture (preview and video recording confirmed; stills not explicitly tested yet)
[*]FM Radio
[*]Bluetooth pairing / A2DP audio / file transfer (basic on/off + discovery confirmed; full pairing flow not yet tested end-to-end)
[/LIST]

[B]Known bugs[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Calls do not work — rild crash loop[/B] — [I]requestRadioPower[/I] NULL pointer dereference in mtk-ril.so, confirmed via tombstone. Telephony is not usable on this build yet.
[*][B]Video recording stops itself after a few seconds[/B] — an AudioFlinger RecordThread buffer overflow triggers a MediaRecorder error mid-recording; the in-progress file gets discarded. Recording genuinely works up to that point (real audio + video captured), it just doesn't run indefinitely yet. Likely a scheduling/priority issue between the audio capture thread and the encoder on this modest single/dual-core SoC while also driving camera preview + video encode simultaneously.
[*][B]No on-device shell scripting[/B] — mksh and busybox's ash both segfault on ANY invocation on this build, even a trivial "echo hi". Does not affect normal use (nothing in the shipped ROM depends on shell scripts), but rules out on-device init.d scripts and most command-line debugging tricks.
[*][B]Cosmetic: TWRP dmesg shows "init: cannot expand '${ro.serialno}'"[/B] — harmless; the bootloader doesn't pass a serial number to the minimal recovery ramdisk, so `adb devices` shows a placeholder serial in recovery only.
[*][B]Cosmetic: missing spinner animation frame[/B] in TWRP's portrait_mdpi theme ("indeterminate013" not found).
[*][B]Rare one-time ADB drop shortly after boot[/B] — not fully explained, doesn't recur once past it, doesn't affect normal use.
[/LIST]

[B]Important notes[/B]
[LIST]
[*]This ROM is for [B]LG-E440g / vee4ss ONLY[/B]. Do not flash on any other L4 II variant.
[*][B]This is an alpha build — no calls, SMS, or mobile data yet.[/B] Only flash this if you're testing/developing, not as a daily driver.
[*]TWRP recovery required — standard CWM does not support the MTK EMMC partition layout on this device.
[*][B]The OTA zip updates /system only.[/B] You must flash boot.img separately via dd (see Install instructions).
[*]Make a full Nandroid backup before flashing.
[*]Back up your NVRAM partition to protect your IMEI and calibration data before testing any MTK ROM.
[*]This device has no standard fastboot (MTK) — flashing recovery/boot images is done via dd from a rooted Android/TWRP shell, not fastboot.
[*][B]After first boot, go to Settings → Bluetooth → Rename this device once[/B] (even to the same name). Android doesn't push your device name to the Bluetooth chip until you do this explicitly — until then, other devices scanning for you will see a generic "MTK MT6620 #N" instead of your real device name. This is normal Android behavior, not specific to this ROM.
[*]GApps: use a Jelly Bean compatible package.
[/LIST]

[B]Requirements[/B]
[LIST]
[*]LG-E440g (vee4ss) — tested hardware only
[*]TWRP recovery (MTK-compatible build for this device)
[*]At least 30% battery charge
[*]Full Nandroid backup (strongly recommended)
[/LIST]

