[B]Source / build[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Android base: CyanogenMod 10 / Android 4.1.2
[*]Device tree: device/lge/vee4ss (branch jellybean)
[*]Vendor blobs: extracted from stock LG-E440g firmware (JZO54K)
[*]Kernel: stock prebuilt (MT6575, Linux 3.4.x), MTK header re-added at build time via mtkbootimg
[*]Boot image: generated with mtkbootimg
[*]Build date: 2026-07-30
[/LIST]

[B]Changelog[/B]

[B]2026-07-30 — Build 2[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Camera recording crash fixed[/B] — `CameraSource::getColorFormat()` crashed on a NULL `video-frame-format` HAL parameter (this HAL never sets that key); now defaults safely to the HAL's actual YUV420 semi-planar preview format.
[*][B]Second recording crash fixed[/B] — `AudioSource`'s destructor could `delete` an uninitialized pointer when the audio config negotiation failed partway through construction; now safely initialized to NULL.
[*][B]Fixed broken default video-quality profile[/B] — the Camera app was requesting a 720p profile this device's `media_profiles.xml` never defined; tuned the "high" profile's audio codec settings (sample rate / channel count) to match what this device's audio HAL actually supports.
[*][B]MAJOR: fixed total audio failure (input AND output)[/B] — the stock audio HAL blob's internal module identifier was baked in as "libaudio" instead of the expected "audio", so the audio framework silently refused to load it on every single boot. Audio never worked on this device before this fix. Disabled the (now-inapplicable) strict module-id check for this device only.
[*]Video recording now genuinely starts and captures real audio + video (known remaining bug: stops itself after a few seconds, see Known bugs).
[/LIST]

[B]2026-07-29 — Build 1 (initial public test)[/B]
[LIST]
[*]First build with a working display on this device. Root cause of the long-standing black-screen issue: this device's proprietary MTK graphics blobs use MediaTek's own extensions to the stock Jelly Bean HWC/GraphicBuffer ABI, absent from plain AOSP/CM10. Added a compatibility shim (scoped to this device only) restoring the extra fields and the private presentation flag the blob expects, plus the decisive fix in SurfaceFlinger's `HWComposer.cpp` (setting the vendor HWC's private `LAYERS_SWAP_REQUIRED` list bit before `set()`).
[*]Bluetooth (MT6620 BlueAngel stack) brought up — MediaTek's proprietary Bluetooth integration added to the framework, `servicemanager` updated to allow the Bluetooth UID to register its profile services. Confirmed full on/off cycle and classic discovery.
[*]Based on the already hardware-verified vee5ss device tree (same MT6575 SoC family, same LG generation) — most fixes transferred cleanly; the remaining differences are this device's smaller HVGA command-mode panel vs. vee5ss's WVGA video-mode panel, and per-device audio/USB IDs.
[/LIST]

